# {{name}}

{{description}}

This example is a DGK workbench: it imports neutral capability host blocks, declares
one product/persona verb (`{{personaVerb}}`), and lets the host project the same
capabilities across CLI, HTTP, TUI-ready actions, and agent surfaces.

The generated CLI is a thin white-label host. Manual dispatch goes through an
isolated compatible sidecar by default, so the example exercises the same daemon
path a power user extension would use.

```bash
pnpm --filter {{name}} run build
pnpm --filter {{name}} run {{commandName}} -- {{personaVerb}} --json
pnpm --filter {{name}} run {{commandName}} -- actions --json
```

Set `{{constantName}}_SIDECAR_URL` to point this example at its isolated demo
runtime. If unset, `{{commandName}}` targets `http://127.0.0.1:{{runtimeSidecarPort}}`.
